// Native marker targets, addressable by name from strike_bond.lua's presentation{markers=...}.
//
// Garden published no markers at all: Controller::publish called objectives_.set(event) with no
// target, and ObjectiveService::set OVERWRITES state_.marker with whatever it is handed - so every
// directive change wiped the waypoint, and the standalone .marker mechanic only survived until the
// next objective. gateway, strike_pact, deep_storage and deadly_trial all bind the marker TO the
// objective instead; this is that table for Garden.
//
// The four locator words carry the packaged FNV absent sentinel, exactly as strike_pact's
// kAbsentLocator does. Zero is a legal locator value and would read as a supplied position, so an
// unused slot must be the sentinel and NOT zero.
inline constexpr std::array<std::uint32_t,4> kAbsentLocator{0x811C9DC5U,0x811C9DC5U,0x811C9DC5U,0x811C9DC5U};
